# Kindred Editorial Constitution

**Trust is our most valuable feature.**

**Universal craft standard:** `kindred-newspaper-editorial-standards.mdc` — how every
article is written (lead with the news, build understanding, trust over length).
**Local identity standard:** `kindred-local-business-first.mdc` — what makes a city
worth experiencing (local business first when quality is comparable).
This file covers **what may be published** and verification gates.

Kindred **NEVER** guesses, assumes, fabricates, or fills missing information
with AI inference. If something cannot be verified with sufficient confidence,
**it is not published.**

**Accuracy always beats quantity.** A smaller newspaper with 25 verified events
is better than 40 events containing one incorrect listing. The same rule applies
to Activities and Recommendations.

**When in doubt: LEAVE IT OUT.** Every pick should be accurate enough that we
would confidently send our own family there.

## Before publication — verify

### Events

- Date, time, timezone
- Venue
- Official website
- Maps coordinates
- Event status (not cancelled / postponed / registration closed)
- Source agreement (no conflicting dates across sources)
- **Editorial copy:** original summary + Bandit's Note — no templates (`kindred-event-editorial.mdc`)

**Gate:** `localEvents/eventDateVerification.ts` · `editorial/confidence.ts` ·
`localEvents/familyFriendlyFilter.ts` (before dedupe + rank) · pipeline +
`buildEdition.ts` publish re-check. Only `verificationStatus = "verified"` enters
the edition.

### Family-Friendly Discovery Standard (permanent)

Kindred is a **family-friendly discovery platform** that helps people discover
the best experiences in their city. This rule is **not** based on whether an
event is 21+, politics, viewpoints, or popularity. It **is** based on whether
the **primary purpose** of the venue or event aligns with Kindred's mission of
helping people discover the best places in their city.

**Allow when editorial quality is high:** restaurants · breweries · wineries ·
cocktail bars · distilleries · coffee shops · fine dining · live music · jazz
clubs · comedy clubs · theater · museums · festivals · farmers markets ·
sporting events · community events · cultural celebrations · casinos (where
legal) · 21+ events that are legitimate entertainment or hospitality
experiences. Rank on quality, verification, editorial value, Local Business First.

**Exclude before ranking:** strip clubs · gentlemen's clubs · adult bookstores ·
pornography or sexually explicit businesses · escort services · sexually themed
venues or performances · drag shows or drag-themed performances · adult novelty
stores · fetish or BDSM events · nude or partially nude entertainment · any
venue whose primary purpose is explicit sexual entertainment. Remove from the
candidate pool entirely — never just lower the score.

**Engineering rule:** age restriction alone must **never** exclude an event.
**Primary purpose** is the determining factor. Legitimate food, culture, music,
comedy, nightlife, hospitality, sports, history, education, or community → may
include. Adult or sexually themed entertainment → remove before ranking so it
never reaches homepage, recommendations, search, affiliate recommendations, or
future city editions. Applies globally across every Kindred edition.

**Surfaces:** Local Events · Activities · Food & Drinks · Bandit's Picks ·
Recommendations · Search · future affiliate recommendations.

**Also exclude (non-adult):** hate groups and extremist rallies; violence or
illegal activity promotion; scams (pyramid schemes, MLM recruiting, timeshare
pitches, get-rich-quick and predatory financial seminars, fake crypto/investment
schemes).

**Diagnostics:** log filtered count, reason (`signal` + `category`), and sample
titles each edition. Provider-agnostic — applies to Eventbrite, Ticketmaster, and
all future sources.

**Gate:** `localEvents/familyFriendlyFilter.ts` (before dedupe + rank) ·
`discovery/score.ts` for Activities, Recommendations, and Bandit's Pick ·
`buildEdition.ts` publish re-check.

### The Kindred Test (permanent — final editorial filter)

Every recommendation must pass one question **after** verification, ranking,
and safety checks:

> "If someone was visiting this city for the first time, would I be genuinely
> excited to recommend this?"

**YES** → may continue through editorial review. **NO** → do not publish, even if
it technically qualifies. Applies to every desk and surface.

**Usually PASS:** beloved neighborhood restaurant · great local brewery · scenic
overlook · museum · concert · farmers market · cultural festival · historic
landmark · unique coffee shop · local bookstore · reputable comedy club ·
highly rated cocktail bar · local art gallery.

**Usually FAIL:** adult or sexually themed venues/performances · strip clubs ·
gentlemen's clubs · drag shows or drag-themed performances · airport terminals ·
office parks · generic chains with no local significance when better locals exist ·
sales seminars · MLM events · spam · placeholders · duplicates · low-quality
filler · anything that makes the city feel less authentic or less welcoming.

Kindred is not trying to list everything. Kindred is trying to recommend the best.

### Activities

- Business exists
- Not permanently closed
- Maps coordinates verified
- Website verified
- Hours verified when available

**Gate:** `editorial/confidence.ts` · `discovery/confidencePayload.ts` ·
place provider verification.

### Recommendations

- Location exists
- Maps coordinates verified
- Official website when applicable
- Business not permanently closed
- Article facts verified

**Gate:** same discovery confidence stack; `familyFriendlyFilter.ts` ·
`contentQuality.ts` · `places/chains.ts` for local-first, verified listings.
**Local Business First:** `kindred-local-business-first.mdc` ·
`localBusinessFirst.ts` · `venueEditorialScore.ts` · `discovery/score.ts` —
when quality and trust are comparable, verified independents rank above chains;
never fabricate local status.

### Maps

Never guess coordinates. Always verify the pin opens at the intended
destination. **If coordinates cannot be verified, do not publish.**

### Articles

See **`kindred-newspaper-editorial-standards.mdc`** for the full 12 editorial
standards (lead with the news, build understanding, write like a newspaper,
trust over length, reader test). That standard applies to **every desk**.

Never invent history, facts, rankings, awards, or claims. Write only from
verified information. If confidence is low, **omit the statement** — do not
soften with speculation.

**Unique Conclusions (Swap Test):** `kindred-unique-conclusions.mdc` — every
long-form article must end with an original conclusion. No reusable paragraphs,
no rotating closing pools, no generic wrap-ups. If the last paragraph could
paste into another article unnoticed, rewrite it.

**Memorable Writing (Lasting Thought Test):** `kindred-memorable-writing.mdc` —
every article must leave the reader with one memorable idea. No filler, no
generic takeaways. If nothing would stick an hour later, rewrite it.

**Today's Masterpiece:** `kindred-masterpiece-editorial.mdc` — museum magazine
structure, facts-first Overview, no cross-section repetition, 1,200–2,000 words
when verified material supports it.

**Gate:** `kindredEditorialStandards.ts` · `storyEditor/` · `editorialStyle.ts` ·
`editorial/confidence.ts` · `uniqueConclusions.ts` ·
`memorableWriting.ts` · `categoryIcon.ts` · hero/detail templates must use verified
library metadata only.

**Visual Language (v1):** `kindred-visual-language.mdc` — one verified category,
one permanent emoji. Never stack. Icon follows the article everywhere.

## General rule

When confidence is below the publishing threshold: **DO NOT PUBLISH.**

Do not backfill sections with questionable content. An empty desk is better
than a wrong one.

## Engineering defaults

| Action | Required behavior |
| --- | --- |
| Missing field | Reject or omit — never invent |
| Low confidence | `action: "reject"` or `"enrich"` — never force `"publish"` |
| Conflicting sources | Reject until resolved |
| AI copy | Enrich verified facts only — never create facts |
| Expired / past event | Remove — never show as upcoming |

Existing patterns to extend, not bypass: `computeEventConfidence`,
`computeDiscoveryConfidence`, `shouldPublishEditorialConfidence`,
`filterVerifiedEventsForEdition`, `filterFamilyFriendlyEvents`,
`assessFamilyFriendlyListing`, `pruneDiscoveryPayloadByConfidence`.
